  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry weather will continue through Sunday night.\n\nChamber of commerce weather will continue through the end of the \nweekend with dry weather and clear skies through Sunday evening. \nTonight will be cool once again, with lows dropping back into the \n30s areawide, and some 20s in the colder Southern Tier Valleys and \nTug Hill region. There may be a small amount of river valley fog \nacross the Southern Tier late tonight through Sunday morning.\n\nFull sunshine will continue Sunday as strong high pressure remains \nanchored along the southern New England coast. Temperatures will be \na few degrees warmer than today, with highs in the mid 60s for lower \nelevations and around 60 on the hilltops.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A cold front will bring a chance of a few scattered \nlight showers to northern New York Monday, followed by a brief \ncooldown Tuesday.\n\nA mid level trough will sharpen and dig southeast across Quebec \nMonday, dragging an associated cold front south across the eastern \nGreat Lakes. The majority of the stronger forcing and deeper \nmoisture will remain displaced well north of the area. A few \nscattered light showers may cross the Saint Lawrence Valley and \nhigher terrain of the North Country. Otherwise, the front will \nlikely pass through the rest of the area dry with nothing more than \nan increase in cloud cover.\n\nCold advection behind the departing front will bring a brief one day \ncooldown Tuesday. Highs will reach the low to mid 50s across Western \nNY and 40s for the North Country. A ridge surface and aloft will \nquickly build back into the eastern CONUS Wednesday and last through \nthe end of next week. This will bring another long period of dry \nweather and above average high temperatures.",
